    "turn_text": "This is Acropulse Drive Time for Monday, July 1st, brought to you by the American Farm Bureau Federation. Good afternoon. I'm Jeff Nally. Well, the USDA's crop condition and progress report today showed another decline in corn condition while soybean condition remained steady. USDA said 67 percent of corn acres rated good to excellent. That's compared to last week 69 percent. And last year's figure of 51 percent for this date. Soybean condition remained at 67% good to excellent. That's 17 points better than a year ago. 11% of the corn crop silking as of Sunday compared to the 6% average. 20% of the soybean crop blooming the same as last year. 5 points better than the 5-year average. Kansas' first district representative Tracy Mann is this week's guest on agriculture newsmakers. Mann says farmers in the big first and across the country cannot continue to wait for a farm bill.",
