    "turn_text": "I authored this legislation called American Farmer Feeds the World and basically it ensures that at least 50% of what we're of the aid we're sending is in commodities, not just money. A problem we have when it's just money as well is that money can end up in other places. It's hard to trace. When it's commodities, one we know it's American grown. It's good for the producer. and to we actually know that food is getting to hungry people and then goes all over the world that goes to africa uh... other countries um... you know ideally these programs are going to places into people that don't aren't able to grow their own calories which is why we got to send in food",
