    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/4/84743.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "and also speaks to c r p rebel rates being proposed to the house g l p farm bill Newsmakers is available this week at www.acropulse.com. The dairy industry is in the process of digesting the USDA's proposal for revising the federal milk marketing order. The USDA's proposal said to be over 300 pages and include plans to revert to the old formula for Class 1 fluid milk pricing. They're also said to be offering adjustments to the make allowances, those deductions for manufacturing costs. The USDA released its planted acreage report last week, but not all planting was done at the time of the survey. While corn planting was higher than the trade anticipated, three and a third billion acres were left to plant. And as for soybeans, there were still 12.8 million acres that were not seeded at the time of collecting data for the report. Today's drive time is brought to you by the American Farm Bureau Federation. Farmers have the right to repair their own equipment thanks to a series of memorandums of understanding between the American Farm Bureau Federation and major agricultural machinery manufacturers, including John Deere, Case IH, New Holland, Kubota, and Agco. Learn more at FB.org slash write to repair. Well, that's all for today's AgriPulse drive time. For more agriculture, trade, food, environment, and regulatory news, visit agriPulse.com. for Adropulse. I'm Jeff Daley.",
